    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0459" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg427"/>

                <head>252. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Jordan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d252-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-08-03T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1958—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>397. Embtel 272.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d252-f2"
                    /> Inform King and Prime Minister we have been giving careful consideration to
                        HKJ proposal for financing two new brigades.
                    As King and Rifai know we continue our firm support for Jordan. We believe
                    however we will be in better position reach decision <pb facs="0460" n="428"
                        xml:id="pg428"/> regarding these brigades when we know results of
                    deliberations of proposed high level SC meeting
                    on ME. If this meeting takes place the security
                    of all states in ME, and especially Jordan and
                    Lebanon, against indirect aggression will be a principal topic of discussion and
                    it is US intention to seek in SC measures and
                    arrangements designed to safeguard ME states
                    against this threat. SC deliberations may thus
                    have important implications for future security of ME states and accordingly we believe we should hold final decision
                    on request for two additional brigades in abeyance pending results SC meeting.</p>
                <p>You should inform King and Rifai that we do not agree that BP “finished” as
                    northern tier defense arrangement. On the contrary, during London BP meeting US
                    strengthened its relationship with northern tier countries and intends increase
                    its support of the defense of these nations. We furthermore doubt that several
                    of countries mentioned by Rifai would be willing join suggested organization.
                    Accordingly while we very much appreciate receiving King’s suggestion it is our
                    view it would not be desirable to seek new regional defense organization at this
                    time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
